From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0380-swap-safe-0182-tell-the-service-where-the-game-pool-lies.patch

Source: 0380-swap-safe-0182-tell-the-service-where-the-game-pool-lies.patch
The guest's memory service may arm only the game's application pool, and only
the kernel knows where that lies. eden_guest_swap_pool is called once the memory
manager is up. Weak, like eden_guest_swap_active (patch 0125): a build without
the PS5 frontend skips the call, and the PS5 link defines it, so it leaves no
undefined weak symbol for headless/check_package.py.

Goes with swap-safe-frontend-03. Telling it changes nothing by itself. No pool
memory.

Source: no upstream PR or commit. From the run 59 analysis.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/core/hle/kernel/kernel.cpp b/src/core/hle/kernel/kernel.cpp
index 9e6ccc2d89..2a9b1a7735 100644
--- a/src/core/hle/kernel/kernel.cpp
+++ b/src/core/hle/kernel/kernel.cpp
@@ -50,6 +50,10 @@
 #include "core/hle/service/sm/sm.h"
 #include "core/memory.h"
 
+// PS5 port (src/guest_memory_service.inc): where the game's pool lies in the guest's backing.
+extern "C" void eden_guest_swap_pool(std::uint64_t offset, std::uint64_t bytes) noexcept
+    __attribute__((weak));
+
 namespace Kernel {
 
 // Can only be used by a single implementation PER THREAD
@@ -749,6 +753,13 @@ struct KernelCore::Impl {
         const auto& management_region = memory_layout->GetPoolManagementRegion();
         ASSERT(management_region.GetEndAddress() != 0);
         memory_manager->Initialize(management_region.GetAddress(), management_region.GetSize());
+
+        // PS5 port: only the game's own pool may lose its mapping for a while. The slab heaps and
+        // the other pools hold objects of this kernel and what the emulator reads all the time.
+        if (eden_guest_swap_pool) {
+            const auto pool = memory_layout->GetKernelApplicationPoolRegionPhysicalExtents();
+            eden_guest_swap_pool(pool.GetAddress() - Core::DramMemoryMap::Base, pool.GetSize());
+        }
     }
 
     void InitializeHackSharedMemory(KernelCore& kernel) {
